    </tr>
    <tr valign="top" style="background:#f0f0f0"> 
      <td>
        <a href="https://arabidopsis.org/servlets/Search?type=general&search_action=detail&method=1&sub_type=gene&SEARCH_EXACT=4&name=KCS3">KCS3</a>
      </td>
      <td><a href="/gene_center/gene/KCS24">kcs24</a></td>
      <td>GRMZM2G894016</td>
      <td>Zm00001d018455</td>
      <td>Zm00001eb258610</td>
      <td>
        The Arabidopsis gene loci KCS3 and KCS5 are represented as the same maize gene 
        locus (kcs24\) and gene model in the B73v4 nnotation. This is because they were 
        originally generated based on the B73v3 annotation. However, KCS3 and KCS5 are 
        different loci.	 
      </td>
      <td>
        For KCS5, the correct v5 gene model is Zm00001eb399930, and the correct v4 
        gene model is Zm00001d048059.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr valign="top"> 
      <td>
        <a href="https://arabidopsis.org/servlets/Search?type=general&search_action=detail&method=1&sub_type=gene&SEARCH_EXACT=4&name=KCS4">KCS4</a>
      </td>
      <td><a href="/gene_center/gene/kcs1">kcs1</a>
      <td> </td>
      <td>Zm00001d009608</td>
      <td>Zm00001eb344080, Zm00001eb344070</td>
      <td>
        Each of the Arabidopsis gene loci KCS4, KCS13, and KCS22 match a different gene model 
        in B73v4. However, in B73v5 they span two gene models. (Zm00001eb398750
        and Zm00001eb398760 for KCS13, Zm00001eb344080 and Zm00001eb344070 for KCS4 and KCS22\).
      </td>
      <td>
        Zm00001eb344080, Zm00001eb344070 are overlapping gene models in v5; 
        Zm00001eb344070 is correct for Arabidposis KCS4 and KCS22 base on orientation with 
        respect to B73v4: https://genomevolution.org/r/1orwt. Zm00001eb398750 and 
        Zm00001eb398760 are also overlapping gene models in B73v5. Zm00001eb398750 is 
        correct for Arabidoposis KCS13 based on orientation with respect to B73v3 ane B73v4.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr valign="top" style="background:#f0f0f0"> 
